# obj.gbnf — v1989: GBNF grammar for llama-server that constrains generation to
# syntactically valid Wavefront OBJ, at the DECODER level. The model literally
# cannot emit markdown fences, prose, negative face indices, or malformed lines —
# every token must extend a valid "v x y z" or "f i j k [l]" line.
#
# Used by OllamaClient.generateOBJ() when a llama-server URL is configured
# (voxelengine.llamaServerUrl). Attacks FailedOBJStore rejects at the source.
# NOTE: grammar guarantees FORMAT, not geometry quality — the QC gate still runs.
#
# llama-server usage: POST /completion { prompt, grammar: <this file's text>, ... }

root   ::= vline vline vline vline+ fline fline+
vline  ::= "v " num " " num " " num "\n"
fline  ::= "f " idx " " idx " " idx (" " idx)? "\n"
num    ::= "-"? int frac?
int    ::= [0-9] | [1-9] [0-9] | [1-9] [0-9] [0-9]
frac   ::= "." [0-9] [0-9]? [0-9]? [0-9]?
idx    ::= [1-9] [0-9]? [0-9]?
